session:pr721Summary a agp:TranscriptSummary ;
    agp:summaryText "Issue #517 asked for OpenAPI coverage of the five route groups #386 deliberately deferred: SHACL, RML, OTTR, the runtime-ruleset endpoint, and the transaction API. Before writing any PathItems, I read server.rs's actual router to confirm all five areas really are wired handlers (they are) rather than trusting the issue's framing. My first draft got two things wrong, each caught on review rather than up front: the rules/transaction handlers return plain application/json (axum Json<...>), but I'd reused the existing ok_json_response helper, which despite its generic name hardcodes application/sparql-results+json — worth flagging for whoever next adds a JSON-returning path, since the helper name doesn't warn you; and the DELETE /{name}/rules/{ruleset_id} handler's 200-body shape was documented without its ruleset_id field, plus its 409 (contradictory remaining ruleset) response was omitted entirely by only reading the 200/403/404 paths on first pass. Separately, txId (the transaction id, checked against the store's generation for optimistic concurrency on commit) is only honored by the root /sparql handler, not the dataset-scoped /{name}/sparql — confirmed by grepping query.rs vs dataset_routes.rs rather than assuming symmetry, so it's documented only on the root path item. Multipart bodies (RML, OTTR) are documented as an opaque multipart/form-data string schema rather than per-part schema, continuing the 'awkward to express cleanly' resolution #386 flagged. Separately, I found several other server.rs routes undocumented (some wrongly claimed covered by the #386 plan doc) and filed them as follow-up #723 rather than scope-creeping this PR." ;
    agp:reasoningFor ghpull:721 ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy session:pr721 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo session:claudeSonnet5 .

session:pr721Summary agp:decisionPoint session:pr721Decision .

session:pr721Decision a agp:Decision ;
    agp:summaryText "Documented the txId (transaction id) query parameter only on the root /sparql path item, not on the dataset-scoped /{name}/sparql and /{name}/query path items that share the same sparql_query_path_item() builder function." ;
    agp:alternative "Adding txId unconditionally to every SPARQL query path item (dataset-scoped included) was the simpler first instinct, since the three routes already share one helper function and one params list. Rejected after grepping query.rs and dataset_routes.rs: only query.rs's root /sparql handler actually reads the txId query parameter; dataset_routes.rs's dataset-scoped handlers never look at it. Documenting it everywhere would have described transactional behavior the dataset-scoped routes don't have, so the parameter is pushed onto the params Vec conditionally on !dataset_scoped instead." .
